  awk 'length>100' BarWidget.qml -> empty; grep -nE ' +$' -> empty; file ends \n

EVIDENCE:
  Wiring: imports QtQuick, qs.Ui, "Model.js" as Model; moduleName =
    "io.github.yadav-prakhar.omafan"; Loader{active:true; visible:false;
    source:Qt.resolvedUrl("Panel.qml")} with injectPanel()/onBarChanged/
    onSettingsChanged; forwards opened/popoutSwitchClosing/open/close/
    togglePanel/closeForPopoutSwitch. No IpcHandler, no Quickshell.Io.
  Glyph: fc-match -f '%{family[0]}' monospace -> MesloLGL Nerd Font;
    fc-list ":family=MesloLGL Nerd Font:charset=f0210" family -> present, so
    the md-fan glyph ("\udb80\ude10", U+F0210) paints in the real bar font.
  Integration: bash tests/manifest.test.sh -> manifest: PASS 23 / FAIL 2; the
    only failures are "Panel.qml exists" (T09) and "README present" (T11). The
    BarWidget.qml assertions (manifest.test.sh:46,50) now pass (was 22/3).
  PlainText: our strings reach Text.PlainText twice — WidgetButton.qml:77
    (label) and Bar.qml:1338 (tooltip) — so no extra Text element was needed.

DECISIONS:
  - Status comes from panelItem.status, the panel's parsed state (DESIGN §6.2
    state list), normalised to accept either the raw omafan.status.v1 document
    or Model.parseStatus()'s {ok,status} wrapper. The bar runs no poller of its
    own: T07 forbids writes and DESIGN §6.1 gives the widget no command child.
  - Every gesture that changes state goes through the panel's command function
    (DESIGN §6.1 "must go through the panel's command function"): wheel sends
    sendCommand(["rpm", "<n>"]), right-click on a hold sends
    sendCommand(["release"]); both guarded with typeof === "function" so a
    missing panel no-ops instead of throwing. sendCommand(args) is called with
    the omafan-ctl arguments after the program name, the panel prepending its
    ctlPath/env (T09, DESIGN R4).
  - Wheel base = hold.rpm while holdActive, else Model.presetRpm("med",...),
    then Model.snapRpm(...,100) (DESIGN §6.1, §3).
  - Tint: button.active = status.hold.active === true, useActiveColor true
    (DESIGN §6.1, §4.1 hold.active derivation).
  - Tooltip = "Fan <formatRpm> · CPU <formatTemp> · <modeTone>", or
    "Fan control" before any panel status (DESIGN §5 formatters, §6.1 shape).
  - show enum: unknown/empty degrades to the documented default temp; missing
    numbers show the glyph rather than a fake "—"; vertical bars show the glyph
    only, matching the shell's own text widgets (shell README, Orientation).

OPEN:
  - Live load / qs log scan is the orchestrator's step only: worker rules forbid
    writing under ~/.config/omarchy, so I could not install/rescan the plugin.
  - Cross-ticket coupling to confirm with T09: sendCommand(args) takes the
    arguments after the ctl path, and its `status` property holds the parsed
    document (or the {ok,status} wrapper). If T09 chose another shape, only
    applyToPanel() and statusDoc need changing. I did not add an
    orchestration/QUESTIONS.md entry because this ticket (and the operator
    instruction) limits edits to BarWidget.qml — please forward this note.
  - Harness defect, not mine: tests/run-all.sh reports SKIP for all six suites
    because run_suite treats $2 as the "present" path while callers pass the
    interpreter (`run_suite "plugin-validate" bash tests/plugin-validate.sh`),
    so `-e bash` is false. That gate currently executes nothing.
